      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Additionally it's been noted in the May 1, 2026 developer Q&A stream: https://ask.vrchat.com/t/may-1-2026-developer-stream-q-a-summary/48386#p-89302-improving-user-privacy-options-avatar-changes-visible-in-api-14\n\n> A: Avatar changes being visible via API is partly intentional - clients need to know what avatar someone is wearing, and restricting that breaks things. The bigger issue is we’ve never formally defined what level of privacy users should expect in VRChat - we haven’t made that promise technologically or via policy, and we need to. That’s something we’re aware of and have to address. [...]",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
